From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 12:36:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msm8994 display: drop libbfqio (removed from LineageOS after
 18.1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

vendor/lineage/libbfqio is a LineageOS compat shim that exists on lineage-18.1 and was removed for
19.1 and later. The msm8994 display HAL still links it and calls android_set_rt_ioprio() from the
vsync thread, so ckati fails:

  hardware/qcom-caf/msm8994/display/libhwcomposer/../common.mk:
    error: "hwcomposer.msm8992 missing libbfqio"

This is exactly what upstream did for msm8996 when carrying it past 18.1 — the commit
'Revert "hwc: Set ioprio for vsync thread"' plus dropping libbfqio from the link list. Found by
diffing lineage-18.1-caf-msm8996 against lineage-20.0-caf-msm8996 before starting this build.

Cost: the vsync thread no longer gets realtime IO priority. Upstream accepted the same trade.
---
 libhwcomposer/Android.mk    | 2 +-
 libhwcomposer/hwc_vsync.cpp | 2 --
 2 files changed, 1 insertion(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libhwcomposer/Android.mk b/libhwcomposer/Android.mk
index 9e6b4a52aa..c4d6be37df 100644
--- a/libhwcomposer/Android.mk
+++ b/libhwcomposer/Android.mk
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@ LOCAL_MODULE_TAGS             := optional
 LOCAL_SHARED_LIBRARIES        := $(common_libs) libEGL liboverlay \
                                  libhdmi libqdutils libhardware_legacy \
                                  libdl libmemalloc libqservice libsync \
-                                 libbinder libmedia libbfqio
+                                 libbinder libmedia
 
 ifeq ($(TARGET_USES_QCOM_BSP),true)
 LOCAL_SHARED_LIBRARIES += libhwui
diff --git a/libhwcomposer/hwc_vsync.cpp b/libhwcomposer/hwc_vsync.cpp
index 275ff371e5..ea3f672d3b 100644
--- a/libhwcomposer/hwc_vsync.cpp
+++ b/libhwcomposer/hwc_vsync.cpp
@@ -18,7 +18,6 @@
  * limitations under the License.
  */
 
-#include <bfqio/bfqio.h>
 #include <cutils/properties.h>
 #include <utils/Log.h>
 #include <fcntl.h>
@@ -119,7 +118,6 @@ static void *vsync_loop(void *param)
     if (sched_setscheduler(gettid(), SCHED_FIFO, &sched_param) != 0) {
         ALOGE("Couldn't set SCHED_FIFO for hwc_vsync");
     }
-    android_set_rt_ioprio(0, 1);
 
     char vdata[MAX_DATA];
     //Number of physical displays
